// stdlib/darwin_pbpk/ddi/multidrug28.sio — dynamic multi-drug interaction driver
// on the PBPK28 (14 organs × {vascular, interstitial}) kernel.
//
// Each drug owns a PBPK28 state and is advanced by the pbpk28_hepatic kernel
// (portal routing, interstitial metabolic sinks): by default with the
// clamp-free TR-BDF2 step and a backward-Euler restart after every dosing
// event (see "Transport" below). Drugs interact
// only through shared enzymes: at site s ∈ {liver (organ 1), gut (organ 8)} the
// intrinsic clearance of victim i by enzyme k is scaled by the reversible
// competitive factor
//
//     f_{i,k,s} = 1 / (1 + L_{k,s} + Σ_{j≠i, Ki_{j,k}>0} C_u,j,s / Ki_{j,k})
//
// with the enzyme-site unbound concentration taken from the INTERSTITIAL layer,
//     C_u,j,s = fu_{j,s} · C_t,j[organ(s)] / K_p,j[organ(s)],
// the same convention the kernel's sink uses (k_t = CLint_u·fu/K_p), so a drug
// "sees" at the enzyme exactly the concentration it is metabolised from.
// L_{k,s} is an optional constant external inhibitor load Σ I/Ki (used by the
// static-limit gate). Self-inhibition (saturable kinetics) is not modelled here.
//
// Transport (md.method). Default md_method_trbdf2(): each step of a drug is
// one TR-BDF2 step (γ = 2 − √2; L-stable, second order, no negativity floor,
// fails closed on an entry below −tol·scale; derivation in the TR-BDF2
// section of pbpk28_hepatic.sio), except that the first step after a dosing
// event of that drug is two backward-Euler half-steps (the restart, below).
// This is method 6 of
// docs/audit/PBPK28_CN_FLOOR_CLAMP_MASS_INJECTION_DISPATCH_2026-09-26.md.
// md_method_cn_legacy() keeps the previous transport -- the floored CN step
// and a floored backward-Euler pair after events -- for old-path controls and
// order studies; its clamped mass is booked in `clamped` (md_clamped). The
// floor injects mass whenever CN's weakly damped stiff modes go negative
// (dispatch: +28 % blood AUC at dt = 0.05 h after a rapamycin bolus); the
// default path has no floor, so `clamped` stays 0.
//
// Quadrature. Blood AUC and elimination (central CL and every sink) are
// accumulated with the weights of the step actually taken, on (x_n, interior
// point, x_{n+1}): TR-BDF2 (w, w, d) with w = 1/(2(2−γ)), d = (1−γ)/(2−γ) on
// (x_n, x_γ, x_{n+1}); the restart (0, 1/2, 1/2) on (x_n, midpoint, x_{n+1});
// legacy CN (1/2, 0, 1/2). With those weights each step satisfies
// x_{n+1} − x_n = dt·A·(quadrature of x) + dt·b exactly, so
//   body + lumen + unabsorbed + eliminated = administered
// holds to rounding at any dt (a trapezoid over a TR-BDF2 trajectory would not;
// the dispatch's "second, independent error").
//
// Coupling across drugs per step (dt):
//   1. oral absorption from each lumen into gut tissue (organ 8), integrated
//      exactly over the step (lumen·(1 - e^{-ka·dt})), held as a constant input
//      over the whole step (both stages, or both restart half-steps);
//   2. factors f^n from the states at t_n;
//   3. predictor: step every drug over dt (its own method: restart or
//      TR-BDF2) with f^n; factors f* from the predicted end states;
//      f^{n+1/2} = (f^n + f*)/2;
//   4. corrector: step every drug from t_n with f^{n+1/2}.
// The factors -- hence each drug's matrix -- are held constant across the
// whole step, both TR-BDF2 stages included. That keeps the two stages on one
// matrix and keeps the quadrature identity above exact; it freezes the
// coefficients at (an O(dt^2) approximation of) the step midpoint, which
// costs O(dt^3) locally, so the coupling is second order. (Evaluating factors
// at the γ-point for stage 1 and at the end for stage 2 would also conserve
// mass -- the identity survives per-stage sinks with the stage-1 weights on
// x_n, x_γ and the stage-2 weight on x_{n+1} -- but gains no order.)
// `iters` sets how many predictor/corrector sweeps are made: 0 is plain Lie
// coupling (f^n frozen, first order), 1 is the predictor-corrector above (the
// default), k > 1 iterates the sweep to its fixed point, the
// midpoint-coefficient coupling f_use = (f^n + f(x_{n+1}))/2 with the same
// transport. The convergence gate uses it as the reference that shares the
// transport discretization.
// Transport is stiff but linear and stays implicit per drug; the interaction is
// nonlinear and is treated explicitly, then corrected.
// Order, as measured by tests/run-pass/darwin_pbpk28_multidrug_order_gates.sio (V5) on
// the physiological transport and the default TR-BDF2 path (2026-09-27, both
// engines): PC against the iterated reference D ratios 3.31, 3.74 (dt 0.02 ->
// 0.005, second order), Lie 2.09, 2.03 (first order); PC self-convergence,
// transport and coupling together, 3.67, 3.82 (dt 0.01 -> 0.00125). On the
// legacy CN path the same study gave 3.89, 3.89 / 1.96, 1.99 / 3.58, 3.77.
// How small dt must be before the ratios settle is set by the strength of the
// interaction nonlinearity, not by transport stiffness (adversarial review,
// 2026-09-26, on the CN path: backward-Euler transport and a 100x smaller lung
// PS leave the ratios unchanged; with the perpetrator dose cut from 100 to
// 10 mg the PC ratios are 3.87-3.93 from dt = 0.04 h down). With strong
// inhibition (C_u/Ki ~ 20) the ratios only settle below dt ~ 0.003 h; at
// dt = 0.02 h the PC error is still ~500 times below Lie's (V5b).
//
// Restart. TR-BDF2's first stage is a CN step of length γ·dt and rings on a
// jump in the state or the input; two backward-Euler half-steps (R(∞) = 0)
// absorb the jump first. The restart is scheduled PER DRUG. A dosing event
// of drug j (oral dose, IV bolus, change of IV rate) schedules it for j and
// for every drug i != j whose transport the event makes non-smooth. Drug i's
// equations depend on the other drugs only through its sinks
// k_t,i,s = fu·Σ_k CLint_i,s,k·f_i,s,k / K_p, and f_i,s,k depends on drug j
// exactly when Ki_j,k > 0. The event makes j's enzyme-site concentration
// non-smooth (a bolus: a kink and a seconds-scale exchange transient; an oral
// dose or a rate change: a jump in its derivative), so i's matrix inherits
// that non-smoothness iff
//   there is an enzyme k with Ki_j,k > 0 and CLint_i,s,k > 0 at some site s.
// Every other drug keeps TR-BDF2, and its trajectory is bit-identical to a run
// without j's event (gate V6e). The rule reads Ki and CLint at the time of the
// dosing call. It was a single global flag before 2026-09-27: dosing any drug
// switched every drug's next step to the restart, so a co-drug dose changed an
// uncoupled victim through the integrator alone (PR #2695 review).
// Finitely many first-order restart steps keep the global order at two
// (Rannacher 1984, Numer. Math. 43:309-327).
//
// Engine note: under the default Madaros engine every struct literal with
// array fields, every local coefficient array and the old portal block's
// state/array copies cost a slot in a handle table that is never reclaimed
// (capacity 2^22; exit 182 "handles full",
// docs/audit/MADAROS_HANDLE_TABLE_182_LIFETIME_DISPATCH_2026-08-17.md). The
// first version of this driver used ~73 handles per step for two drugs and died
// after ~57,500 steps. The step now works in persistent scratch (fields below,
// and PBPK28Work for the kernel). Measured 2026-09-26 on the committed Madaros
// ELF: two drugs run 2.5 million steps and fifteen drugs 14 days at
// dt = 0.02 h without exhaustion; per-construct probes of the step path
// (kernel with and without portal routing, struct copies from fields) allocate
// nothing over 5 million calls.
//
// Layout note: every per-drug quantity is a FLAT f64 array indexed
// [drug·14 + organ], [drug·8 + site·4 + enzyme], [drug·4 + enzyme] or [drug].
// Arrays of structs are avoided on purpose: measured 2026-09-26, a struct array
// built with a repeat initializer ([mk(); N]) aliases all elements under the
// committed Madaros prebuilt, and a write through `bag.st[i].field` is silently
// discarded (or kills the process via `&!`) under lean_single. Flat f64 arrays in
// a struct, mutated through `&!`, are correct on both engines.

use darwin_pbpk::core::pbpk28_params::*
use darwin_pbpk::pbpk28_hepatic::*
use eisa::format::{is_finite_f64}

const MD_MAX: i32 = 16
const MD_NE: i32 = 4
const MD_NS: i32 = 2

// Enzyme and site codes.
pub fn md_cyp3a4() -> i32 { return 0 }
pub fn md_cyp2d6() -> i32 { return 1 }
pub fn md_cyp2c9() -> i32 { return 2 }
pub fn md_cyp2c19() -> i32 { return 3 }
pub fn md_site_liver() -> i32 { return 0 }
pub fn md_site_gut() -> i32 { return 1 }

fn md_site_organ(site: i32) -> i32 { if site == 0 { return 1 } return 8 }

// Transport methods (MultiDrug28.method).
pub fn md_method_trbdf2() -> i32 { return 0 }
pub fn md_method_cn_legacy() -> i32 { return 1 }

pub struct MultiDrug28 {
    pub n: i32,
    pub portal: bool,
    pub iters: i32,           // coupling sweeps: 0 Lie, 1 predictor-corrector, >1 iterated
    pub method: i32,          // transport: md_method_trbdf2() (default) or md_method_cn_legacy()
    // transport parameters, [drug·14 + organ]
    pub v_ref: [f64; 224],
    pub vasc_frac: [f64; 224],
    pub kp: [f64; 224],
    pub ps: [f64; 224],
    pub q: [f64; 224],
    pub cl_central: [f64; 16],
    // enzyme-site parameters
    pub fu_site: [f64; 32],   // [drug·2 + site] unbound fraction at the enzyme site
    pub clint: [f64; 128],    // [drug·8 + site·4 + enz] unbound intrinsic clearance (L/h)
    pub ki: [f64; 64],        // [drug·4 + enz] competitive Ki (unbound, mg/L); <= 0: not an inhibitor
    pub ext_load: [f64; 8],   // [site·4 + enz] constant external load Σ I/Ki
    // absorption and dosing
    pub fa: [f64; 16],
    pub ka: [f64; 16],        // 1/h
    pub iv_rate: [f64; 16],   // mg/h into blood
    // state
    pub cv: [f64; 224],
    pub ct: [f64; 224],
    pub lumen: [f64; 16],     // mg awaiting absorption (already × fa)
    // accounting
    pub dose_in: [f64; 16],   // mg administered (oral + IV)
    pub lost: [f64; 16],      // mg never absorbed ((1 - fa) × oral dose)
    pub elim: [f64; 16],      // mg eliminated (central CL + all sinks)
    pub auc_b: [f64; 16],     // blood AUC (mg·h/L), quadrature of the step taken (see header)
    pub clamped: [f64; 16],   // mg added by the kernel's negativity clamp (legacy path only; 0 = exact)
    pub neg_min_rel: [f64; 16], // most negative entry / scale of any stage or step (clamp-free path; <= 0)
    pub t: f64,
    pub restart: [f64; 16],   // 1.0: the drug's next step is the backward-Euler restart (see header)
    pub stepped: f64,         // 1.0 once any step has been taken (kinetic setters then restart)
    // step scratch (not model state): persistent so that a step allocates no
    // managed handles under Madaros (see the engine note in the header)
    pub f_n: [f64; 128],      // factors at t_n
    pub f_star: [f64; 128],   // factors of the predicted state
    pub f_use: [f64; 128],    // factors the step is taken with
    pub ct_pred: [f64; 224],  // predicted interstitial layer
    pub gut_rate: [f64; 16],  // absorption input of this step (mg/h)
    pub sc_p: PBPKParams28,
    pub sc_s0: PBPKState28,   // drug state at t_n
    pub sc_s: PBPKState28,    // drug state being stepped
    pub sc_h: PBPK28Hepatic,
    pub sc_i: PBPK28Input,
    pub sc_w: PBPK28Work,
}

pub fn md_new(portal: bool) -> MultiDrug28 {
    MultiDrug28 {
        n: 0, portal: portal, iters: 1, method: 0,
        v_ref: [0.0; 224], vasc_frac: [0.0; 224], kp: [0.0; 224], ps: [0.0; 224], q: [0.0; 224],
        cl_central: [0.0; 16],
        fu_site: [0.0; 32], clint: [0.0; 128], ki: [0.0; 64], ext_load: [0.0; 8],
        fa: [0.0; 16], ka: [0.0; 16], iv_rate: [0.0; 16],
        cv: [0.0; 224], ct: [0.0; 224], lumen: [0.0; 16],
        dose_in: [0.0; 16], lost: [0.0; 16], elim: [0.0; 16], auc_b: [0.0; 16], clamped: [0.0; 16],
        neg_min_rel: [0.0; 16], t: 0.0, restart: [0.0; 16], stepped: 0.0,
        f_n: [1.0; 128], f_star: [1.0; 128], f_use: [1.0; 128],
        ct_pred: [0.0; 224], gut_rate: [0.0; 16],
        sc_p: pbpk28_params_rapamycin(), sc_s0: pbpk28_state_zero(), sc_s: pbpk28_state_zero(),
        sc_h: pbpk28_hepatic_none(), sc_i: pbpk28_input_none(), sc_w: pbpk28_work_new(),
    }
}

// Registers a drug; returns its index. fu_b is used for both sites; override the
// gut site with md_set_fu_site (enterocyte convention fu_gut = 1.0).
//
// p.cl_central must carry ONLY the clearance this driver does not model as an
// enzyme sink (renal, biliary, proteolytic, or metabolism by an enzyme outside
// the four here). It is copied unchanged. The stock profiles do not satisfy
// that: pbpk28_params_rapamycin()'s cl_central = 12.4 L/h IS its hepatic CYP3A4
// clearance (core/pbpk28_params.sio), so registering that profile as it stands
// and then calling md_set_clint for the liver counts hepatic elimination twice.
// Set p.cl_central to the residual before registering -- the gates in
// tests/run-pass/darwin_pbpk28_*_gates.sio all overwrite it for this reason.
// Domain check of a transport parameter set, as the kernel uses each field.
// Returns 0 when valid, else the first failing field:
//   1 v_ref[o] not finite > 0 (o = 0..13; blood volume divides every blood
//     row, organ volumes split into the two layers);
//   2 cl_central not finite >= 0 (a negative clearance is a mass source);
//   3 kp[o] not finite > 0, organs 1..13 (the kernel divides by K_p);
//   4 ps[o] not finite >= 0, organs 1..13 (0 is a valid "no exchange");
//   5 q[o] not finite >= 0, organs 1..13 (0 is a valid unperfused organ);
//   6 vasc_frac[o] not finite in (0, 1) strictly, organs 1..13. The kernel
//     floors a zero layer volume at 1e-30 L, which makes that layer's rate,
//     hence λ_max and the fail-closed tolerance, ~1e30 times larger (the
//     check becomes vacuous), while pbpk28_total_mass books the raw zero
//     volume -- so 0 and 1 are rejected here even though the kernel runs;
//   7 an index-0 field the kernel does not read (kp, ps, q, vasc_frac of
//     blood) not finite: they are copied and returned by md_params_of;
//   8 portal routing on and Q_liver < Q_gut + Q_spleen + Q_pancreas (the
//     kernel would panic on the first step; rejected at registration instead).
//   9 v_ref[o]*vasc_frac[o] or v_ref[o]*(1-vasc_frac[o]) < 1e-30, organs
//     1..13 (Copilot review, PR #2695, 2026-10-01, confirmed by direct
//     repro): a v_ref small enough to put either raw layer volume below the
//     kernel's 1e-30 floor is accepted by check 1 (v_ref only needs > 0) and
//     by check 6 (vasc_frac strictly in (0,1) alone does not bound the
//     product), but the solver then computes that layer's rate, hence its
//     whole trajectory, as if the volume were the floored 1e-30 -- while
//     pbpk28_total_mass (core/pbpk28_params.sio) books the true, unfloored
//     volume, the same split check 6 already documents for vasc_frac = 0/1.
//     Measured: v_ref[1] = 1e-32 (vasc_frac unchanged) passes checks 1-8,
//     and one 0.001 h CN step with no sink or dosing moves total mass by
//     0.23% (5.0 -> 4.988324) and the tissue concentration from 0 to
//     10.169484 -- a real mass-conservation violation, not rounding.
// NaN fails every test (each is written as a negated conjunction).
pub fn md_params_error(p: PBPKParams28, portal: bool) -> i32 with Mut {
    var o: i32 = 0
    while o < 14 {
        if !(is_finite_f64(p.v_ref[o]) && p.v_ref[o] > 0.0) { return 1 }
        o = o + 1
    }
    if !(is_finite_f64(p.cl_central) && p.cl_central >= 0.0) { return 2 }
    o = 1
    while o < 14 {
        if !(is_finite_f64(p.kp[o]) && p.kp[o] > 0.0) { return 3 }
        if !(is_finite_f64(p.ps[o]) && p.ps[o] >= 0.0) { return 4 }
        if !(is_finite_f64(p.q[o]) && p.q[o] >= 0.0) { return 5 }
        if !(is_finite_f64(p.vasc_frac[o]) && p.vasc_frac[o] > 0.0 && p.vasc_frac[o] < 1.0) { return 6 }
        o = o + 1
    }
    if !(is_finite_f64(p.kp[0]) && is_finite_f64(p.ps[0]) && is_finite_f64(p.q[0]) && is_finite_f64(p.vasc_frac[0])) { return 7 }
    if portal {
        // The kernel's own expression (pbpk28_hepatic_artery_flow panics on a
        // negative value), so validation and kernel round identically.
        if !(pbpk28_hepatic_artery_flow_unchecked(p) >= 0.0) { return 8 }
    }
    o = 1
    while o < 14 {
        let vv_raw = p.v_ref[o] * p.vasc_frac[o]
        let vt_raw = p.v_ref[o] * (1.0 - p.vasc_frac[o])
        if !(vv_raw >= 1.0e-30 && vt_raw >= 1.0e-30) { return 9 }
        o = o + 1
    }
    return 0
}

pub fn md_add_drug(md: &!MultiDrug28, p: PBPKParams28, fu_b: f64, fa: f64, ka: f64) -> i32 with Mut, Panic {
    let i = (*md).n
    if i >= MD_MAX { panic("multidrug28: more than 16 drugs") }
    // Out-of-range values would create negative mass: fa outside [0, 1] makes
    // the lumen or the unabsorbed pool negative, ka < 0 makes the absorbed
    // amount negative, fu_b outside (0, 1] is not a fraction.
    if !(fu_b > 0.0 && fu_b <= 1.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_add_drug needs 0 < fu_b <= 1") }
    if !(fa >= 0.0 && fa <= 1.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_add_drug needs 0 <= fa <= 1") }
    if !(is_finite_f64(ka) && ka >= 0.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_add_drug needs a finite ka >= 0") }
    if md_params_error(p, (*md).portal) != 0 { panic("multidrug28: md_add_drug: transport parameters out of domain (see md_params_error)") }
    var o: i32 = 0
    while o < 14 {
        (*md).v_ref[i * 14 + o] = p.v_ref[o]
        (*md).vasc_frac[i * 14 + o] = p.vasc_frac[o]
        (*md).kp[i * 14 + o] = p.kp[o]
        (*md).ps[i * 14 + o] = p.ps[o]
        (*md).q[i * 14 + o] = p.q[o]
        o = o + 1
    }
    (*md).cl_central[i] = p.cl_central
    (*md).fu_site[i * 2] = fu_b
    (*md).fu_site[i * 2 + 1] = fu_b
    (*md).fa[i] = fa
    (*md).ka[i] = ka
    (*md).n = i + 1
    return i
}

// Index validation. Every per-drug quantity is a flat array, so an index that
// is out of range for its dimension but still inside the array silently writes
// ANOTHER drug's slot: drug 0 with site 2 lands on drug 1's liver fraction,
// drug 0 with enzyme 4 on drug 1's first Ki. These reject that before the write.
fn md_check_drug(md: &MultiDrug28, drug: i32) with Panic {
    if drug < 0 || drug >= (*md).n { panic("multidrug28: drug index is not a registered drug") }
}

fn md_check_site(site: i32) with Panic {
    if site < 0 || site >= MD_NS { panic("multidrug28: site must be md_site_liver() or md_site_gut()") }
}

fn md_check_enz(enz: i32) with Panic {
    if enz < 0 || enz >= MD_NE { panic("multidrug28: enzyme code out of range") }
}

// Kinetic setters after integration has started (PR #2695 review). A change of
// fu, CLint, Ki or an external load moves sink coefficients, which is a
// discontinuity in the operator of every drug whose sink it touches; TR-BDF2
// applied across it rings exactly as it does after a dose. So once a step has
// been taken, a setter that actually changes a value schedules the
// backward-Euler restart for each affected drug (md_restart_sinks_at). Before
// the first step nothing has been integrated and nothing is scheduled, so
// setup order leaves trajectories bit-identical; a call that writes the value
// already stored is not an event either.
//
// Affected drugs: md_set_clint(i, s, k) and md_set_fu_site(i, s) change drug
// i's own sink at site s; fu also scales i's contribution C_u = fu·C_t/K_p to
// the inhibitor load at site s, so every drug with CLint at that site on an
// enzyme i inhibits is affected too. md_set_ki(j, k) changes the factor of
// every other drug with CLint on enzyme k at either site -- whatever the sign
// of the old or new Ki, which covers switching inhibition on and off.
// md_set_ext_load(s, k) changes the factor of every drug with CLint at (s, k).
fn md_restart_sinks_at(md: &!MultiDrug28, skip: i32, site: i32, enz: i32) with Mut {
    let n = (*md).n
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        if i != skip {
            var hit = false
            if site < 0 {
                if (*md).clint[i * 8 + enz] > 0.0 || (*md).clint[i * 8 + 4 + enz] > 0.0 { hit = true }
            } else {
                if (*md).clint[i * 8 + site * 4 + enz] > 0.0 { hit = true }
            }
            if hit { (*md).restart[i] = 1.0 }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
}

pub fn md_set_fu_site(md: &!MultiDrug28, drug: i32, site: i32, fu: f64) with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, drug)
    md_check_site(site)
    if !(fu > 0.0 && fu <= 1.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_set_fu_site needs 0 < fu <= 1") }
    if fu == (*md).fu_site[drug * 2 + site] { return }
    (*md).fu_site[drug * 2 + site] = fu
    if (*md).stepped != 0.0 {
        (*md).restart[drug] = 1.0
        var k: i32 = 0
        while k < MD_NE {
            if (*md).ki[drug * 4 + k] > 0.0 { md_restart_sinks_at(md, drug, site, k) }
            k = k + 1
        }
    }
}

// clint_u < 0 would make the interstitial sink a mass SOURCE.
pub fn md_set_clint(md: &!MultiDrug28, drug: i32, site: i32, enz: i32, clint_u: f64) with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, drug)
    md_check_site(site)
    md_check_enz(enz)
    if !(is_finite_f64(clint_u) && clint_u >= 0.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_set_clint needs a finite CLint_u >= 0") }
    if clint_u == (*md).clint[drug * 8 + site * 4 + enz] { return }
    (*md).clint[drug * 8 + site * 4 + enz] = clint_u
    if (*md).stepped != 0.0 { (*md).restart[drug] = 1.0 }
}

// A finite Ki <= 0 stays the documented way to declare "not an inhibitor of
// this enzyme". A non-finite Ki is rejected: NaN would disable inhibition
// silently (NaN > 0 is false) and +Inf would be an undocumented second sentinel.
pub fn md_set_ki(md: &!MultiDrug28, drug: i32, enz: i32, ki_u: f64) with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, drug)
    md_check_enz(enz)
    if !is_finite_f64(ki_u) { panic("multidrug28: md_set_ki needs a finite Ki (use Ki <= 0 for no inhibition)") }
    if ki_u == (*md).ki[drug * 4 + enz] { return }
    (*md).ki[drug * 4 + enz] = ki_u
    if (*md).stepped != 0.0 { md_restart_sinks_at(md, drug, 0 - 1, enz) }
}

// load < 0 would raise the factor above 1 (a competitive ACTIVATOR), and
// load <= -1 would make the denominator 1 + load zero or negative.
pub fn md_set_ext_load(md: &!MultiDrug28, site: i32, enz: i32, load: f64) with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_site(site)
    md_check_enz(enz)
    if !(is_finite_f64(load) && load >= 0.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_set_ext_load needs a finite load >= 0") }
    if load == (*md).ext_load[site * 4 + enz] { return }
    (*md).ext_load[site * 4 + enz] = load
    if (*md).stepped != 0.0 { md_restart_sinks_at(md, 0 - 1, site, enz) }
}

// A dosing event of drug j schedules the backward-Euler restart for the next
// step of j and of every drug whose transport it makes non-smooth (the
// propagation rule is derived in the header, "Restart"). A call that adds
// nothing is not an event: a zero dose, or a rate equal to the current one,
// returns before touching any state, so it leaves the trajectory bit-identical
// to no call. A real change of infusion rate is a step discontinuity in the
// input and still schedules the restart.
fn md_mark_restart(md: &!MultiDrug28, j: i32) with Mut {
    (*md).restart[j] = 1.0
    let n = (*md).n
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        if i != j {
            var coupled = false
            var k: i32 = 0
            while k < MD_NE {
                if (*md).ki[j * 4 + k] > 0.0 {
                    if (*md).clint[i * 8 + k] > 0.0 || (*md).clint[i * 8 + 4 + k] > 0.0 { coupled = true }
                }
                k = k + 1
            }
            if coupled { (*md).restart[i] = 1.0 }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
}

// True when drug i's next step is the backward-Euler restart.
pub fn md_restart_pending(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> bool with Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    return (*md).restart[i] != 0.0
}

// The dose domain shared by the predicates and the dosing calls: a finite
// mg >= 0. Zero is admissible (a no-op).
fn md_dose_mg_ok(mg: f64) -> bool {
    return is_finite_f64(mg) && mg >= 0.0
}

// Whether md_dose_oral / md_dose_iv_bolus would accept a dose of mg: true
// exactly when the call returns normally, because each dosing call panics
// on precisely `!predicate` (after the same index check) before mutating
// anything. The predicate checks the dose domain first (md_dose_mg_ok, the
// one helper the calls use): until 2026-09-27 it checked only overflow, so a
// finite negative dose that the call rejects answered true (PR #2695
// review). It then checks that every cumulative quantity the call updates
// stays finite (lumen, never absorbed, administered; blood concentration and
// administered). Each is a sum of finite doses and can overflow to +Inf: two
// oral doses of 1e308 made `administered` +Inf and the call returned
// normally (PR #2695 review). Exposed so that a gate can test it (a panic
// cannot be observed by the run-pass harness).
// Both validate the drug index like every other public per-drug function
// (md_check_drug): an unregistered slot below capacity would otherwise answer
// from zero-filled storage -- measured 2026-09-27 on slot 3 of a one-drug
// driver, oral "ok", bolus "not ok" (5 mg divided by a zero volume); PR #2695
// review.
pub fn md_oral_dose_ok(md: &MultiDrug28, drug: i32, mg: f64) -> bool with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, drug)
    if !md_dose_mg_ok(mg) { return false }
    let fa = (*md).fa[drug]
    return is_finite_f64((*md).lumen[drug] + fa * mg) && is_finite_f64((*md).lost[drug] + (1.0 - fa) * mg) && is_finite_f64((*md).dose_in[drug] + mg)
}

pub fn md_bolus_dose_ok(md: &MultiDrug28, drug: i32, mg: f64) -> bool with Mut, Div, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, drug)
    if !md_dose_mg_ok(mg) { return false }
    return is_finite_f64((*md).cv[drug * 14] + mg / (*md).v_ref[drug * 14]) && is_finite_f64((*md).dose_in[drug] + mg)
}

pub fn md_dose_oral(md: &!MultiDrug28, drug: i32, mg: f64) with Mut, Panic {
    if !md_oral_dose_ok(md, drug, mg) {
        if !md_dose_mg_ok(mg) { panic("multidrug28: md_dose_oral needs a finite mg >= 0") }
        panic("multidrug28: md_dose_oral: cumulative dose accounting would overflow")
    }
    if mg == 0.0 { return }
    let fa = (*md).fa[drug]
    (*md).lumen[drug] = (*md).lumen[drug] + fa * mg
    (*md).lost[drug] = (*md).lost[drug] + (1.0 - fa) * mg
    (*md).dose_in[drug] = (*md).dose_in[drug] + mg
    // An oral dose is a discontinuity only if drug can actually enter: with
    // fa = 0 everything is booked as never absorbed, and with ka = 0 the lumen
    // never releases. Either way the body's equations are unchanged, so the
    // dose is bookkeeping, not an event (PR #2695 review; gate V6d).
    if fa * mg > 0.0 && (*md).ka[drug] > 0.0 { md_mark_restart(md, drug) }
}

pub fn md_dose_iv_bolus(md: &!MultiDrug28, drug: i32, mg: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    if !md_bolus_dose_ok(md, drug, mg) {
        if !md_dose_mg_ok(mg) { panic("multidrug28: md_dose_iv_bolus needs a finite mg >= 0") }
        panic("multidrug28: md_dose_iv_bolus: blood concentration or dose accounting would overflow")
    }
    if mg == 0.0 { return }
    (*md).cv[drug * 14] = (*md).cv[drug * 14] + mg / (*md).v_ref[drug * 14]
    (*md).dose_in[drug] = (*md).dose_in[drug] + mg
    md_mark_restart(md, drug)
}

// A negative infusion rate would remove body mass and book it as dose.
pub fn md_set_iv_rate(md: &!MultiDrug28, drug: i32, mg_per_h: f64) with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, drug)
    if !(is_finite_f64(mg_per_h) && mg_per_h >= 0.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_set_iv_rate needs a finite mg/h >= 0") }
    if mg_per_h == (*md).iv_rate[drug] { return }
    (*md).iv_rate[drug] = mg_per_h
    md_mark_restart(md, drug)
}

// Both reconstructors validate the drug index: an unregistered slot below
// capacity would otherwise yield zero-filled parameters or state that look valid.
pub fn md_params_of(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> PBPKParams28 with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    var p = pbpk28_params_rapamycin()
    var o: i32 = 0
    while o < 14 {
        p.v_ref[o] = (*md).v_ref[i * 14 + o]
        p.vasc_frac[o] = (*md).vasc_frac[i * 14 + o]
        p.kp[o] = (*md).kp[i * 14 + o]
        p.ps[o] = (*md).ps[i * 14 + o]
        p.q[o] = (*md).q[i * 14 + o]
        o = o + 1
    }
    p.cl_central = (*md).cl_central[i]
    return p
}

pub fn md_state_of(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> PBPKState28 with Mut, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    var s = pbpk28_state_zero()
    var o: i32 = 0
    while o < 14 {
        s.cv[o] = (*md).cv[i * 14 + o]
        s.ct[o] = (*md).ct[i * 14 + o]
        o = o + 1
    }
    return s
}

// exp(-y) for y >= 0: range reduction by halving, Taylor, repeated squaring.
//
// The halving loop cannot make progress for y = +Inf (halving infinity is
// infinity), so it would spin forever. That is reachable from finite inputs:
// ka and dt are each finite but ka·dt can overflow. exp(-y) is exactly 0.0 in
// binary64 for y above ~746, so anything from 750 up -- including +Inf -- takes
// the short-circuit, and every finite y below it needs at most 11 halvings.
fn md_exp_neg(y: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    if y >= 750.0 { return 0.0 }
    if !(is_finite_f64(y) && y >= 0.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_exp_neg needs a finite y >= 0") }
    var z = y
    var m: i32 = 0
    while z > 0.5 {
        z = z * 0.5
        m = m + 1
    }
    var term = 1.0
    var sum = 1.0
    var k: i32 = 1
    while k < 25 {
        term = term * (0.0 - z) / (k as f64)
        sum = sum + term
        k = k + 1
    }
    while m > 0 {
        sum = sum * sum
        m = m - 1
    }
    return sum
}

// Fraction absorbed over a step, 1 - exp(-y) = -expm1(-y), for y = ka·dt >= 0.
// Computing it as 1 - md_exp_neg(y) cancels catastrophically for small y:
// measured 2026-09-27 (PR #2695 review), relative error 2.2e-5 at y = 1e-12,
// 11 % at 1e-16, and a result of exactly 0 at 1e-17 (nothing absorbed). For
// y <= 1/2 the alternating series y - y^2/2 + y^3/6 - ... is summed directly
// (25 terms; the first omitted term is below 0.5^26/26! < 1e-34 of y). Its
// rounding: 4 flops per term, 100 in all, on terms whose absolute sum is
// e^y - 1 = e^y·(1 - e^-y) <= 1.65 times the result, so the relative error
// is below 100·1.65·u ≈ 165u ≈ 3.7e-14. For y > 1/2, exp(-y) <= 0.61 and
// 1 - exp(-y) >= 0.39, so the subtraction amplifies md_exp_neg's relative
// error by at most e^-y/(1 - e^-y) < 1.55 and the range-reduced form is kept.
pub fn md_absorbed_fraction(y: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    if !(y >= 0.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_absorbed_fraction needs y >= 0") }
    if y > 0.5 { return 1.0 - md_exp_neg(y) }
    var term = y
    var sum = y
    var k: i32 = 2
    while k < 26 {
        term = term * (0.0 - y) / (k as f64)
        sum = sum + term
        k = k + 1
    }
    return sum
}

// Inhibitor load L_{i,s,k} = ext_load + Σ_{j≠i, Ki_{j,k}>0} C_u,j,s / Ki_{j,k}
// seen by victim i at (site s, enzyme k), from the state (from_pred = false:
// ct) or the predicted state (true: ct_pred). This is the ONE implementation:
// the step's factors (md_factors_into) and the inspection path
// (md_factor_now) both call it, so they agree by construction.
// The interstitial concentration is floored at zero here, and only here.
// The clamp-free transport tolerates entries down to -tol·scale (rounding),
// and such an entry would make the load negative -- the inhibitor an
// ACTIVATOR, with a factor above 1 (measured 2026-09-27: 1 + 1.85e-11 for
// C_t = -1e-15·C_b with Ki = 1e-6; PR #2695 review). The floor keeps every
// factor in (0, 1]. The state itself is untouched, and so is mass
// conservation, since the factors only scale a sink k >= 0. For
// non-negative concentrations the arithmetic is the same as before, bit for
// bit.
// The sum is checked for overflow, here and therefore on both paths. Every
// input is finite, but the sum need not be: ext_load = 1e308 plus one
// contribution of 1e308 is +Inf, the factor 1/(1 + Inf) is exactly 0, and the
// victim's sink disappears without a word (PR #2695 review). A non-finite load
// panics instead.
fn md_site_load(md: &MultiDrug28, from_pred: bool, i: i32, s: i32, k: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let n = (*md).n
    let o = md_site_organ(s)
    var load = (*md).ext_load[s * 4 + k]
    var j: i32 = 0
    while j < n {
        let kij = (*md).ki[j * 4 + k]
        if j != i && kij > 0.0 {
            let c_raw = if from_pred { (*md).ct_pred[j * 14 + o] } else { (*md).ct[j * 14 + o] }
            let c = if c_raw > 0.0 { c_raw } else { 0.0 }
            let cu = (*md).fu_site[j * 2 + s] * c / (*md).kp[j * 14 + o]
            load = load + cu / kij
        }
        j = j + 1
    }
    if !is_finite_f64(load) { panic("multidrug28: inhibitor load is not finite (overflow in ext_load + sum C_u/Ki)") }
    return load
}

// Competitive factors 1/(1 + load) for every (victim, site, enzyme), in place:
// source layer `from_pred` (false: the state ct, true: ct_pred), destination
// `into_star` (false: f_n, true: f_star).
fn md_factors_into(md: &!MultiDrug28, from_pred: bool, into_star: bool) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let n = (*md).n
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        var s: i32 = 0
        while s < MD_NS {
            var k: i32 = 0
            while k < MD_NE {
                let fk = 1.0 / (1.0 + md_site_load(md, from_pred, i, s, k))
                if into_star { (*md).f_star[i * 8 + s * 4 + k] = fk } else { (*md).f_n[i * 8 + s * 4 + k] = fk }
                k = k + 1
            }
            s = s + 1
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
}

// f_use = f_n (Lie) or (f_n + f_star)/2 (predictor-corrector midpoint).
fn md_set_f_use(md: &!MultiDrug28, midpoint: bool) with Mut {
    var x: i32 = 0
    while x < 128 {
        if midpoint {
            (*md).f_use[x] = 0.5 * ((*md).f_n[x] + (*md).f_star[x])
        } else {
            (*md).f_use[x] = (*md).f_n[x]
        }
        x = x + 1
    }
}

// Loads drug i into the step scratch: parameters, state (twice: t_n and the
// copy being stepped), sinks under f_use, and inputs.
fn md_load(md: &!MultiDrug28, i: i32) with Mut, Div {
    var o: i32 = 0
    while o < 14 {
        (*md).sc_p.v_ref[o] = (*md).v_ref[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_p.vasc_frac[o] = (*md).vasc_frac[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_p.kp[o] = (*md).kp[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_p.ps[o] = (*md).ps[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_p.q[o] = (*md).q[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_s0.cv[o] = (*md).cv[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_s0.ct[o] = (*md).ct[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_s.cv[o] = (*md).cv[i * 14 + o]
        (*md).sc_s.ct[o] = (*md).ct[i * 14 + o]
        o = o + 1
    }
    (*md).sc_p.cl_central = (*md).cl_central[i]
    (*md).sc_h.portal = (*md).portal
    var s: i32 = 0
    while s < MD_NS {
        let org = md_site_organ(s)
        var clint_eff = 0.0
        var k: i32 = 0
        while k < MD_NE {
            clint_eff = clint_eff + (*md).clint[i * 8 + s * 4 + k] * (*md).f_use[i * 8 + s * 4 + k]
            k = k + 1
        }
        (*md).sc_h.k_t[org] = pbpk28_sink_from_clint(clint_eff, (*md).fu_site[i * 2 + s], (*md).kp[i * 14 + org])
        s = s + 1
    }
    (*md).sc_i.in_b = (*md).iv_rate[i]
    (*md).sc_i.in_t[8] = (*md).gut_rate[i]
}

// Steps the loaded drug i in place over dt with its method for this step:
// the backward-Euler restart when one is due, otherwise TR-BDF2 (clamp-free,
// fails closed on negativity) or, on the legacy path, the floored CN step
// (the V0-verified extension of the original kernel) and the floored BE pair.
// Every branch leaves x_n and the interior point in sc_w for md_advance.
fn md_kernel_loaded(md: &!MultiDrug28, i: i32, dt: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let p = (*md).sc_p
    let hep = (*md).sc_h
    let inp = (*md).sc_i
    let rs = (*md).restart[i] != 0.0
    if (*md).method == 1 {
        if rs {
            pbpk28_hepatic_be2_floor_step_ws(&!(*md).sc_s, p, hep, inp, dt, &!(*md).sc_w)
        } else {
            pbpk28_hepatic_cn_step_saved_ws(&!(*md).sc_s, p, hep, inp, dt, &!(*md).sc_w)
        }
    } else {
        if rs {
            pbpk28_hepatic_be2_step_ws(&!(*md).sc_s, p, hep, inp, dt, &!(*md).sc_w)
        } else {
            pbpk28_hepatic_trbdf2_step_ws(&!(*md).sc_s, p, hep, inp, dt, &!(*md).sc_w)
        }
    }
}

// Quadrature weights (x_n, interior, x_{n+1}) of the step drug i takes:
// restart (0, 1/2, 1/2); TR-BDF2 (w, w, d); legacy CN (1/2, 0, 1/2).
fn md_weights(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> (f64, f64, f64) with Div {
    if (*md).restart[i] != 0.0 { return (0.0, 0.5, 0.5) }
    if (*md).method == 1 { return (0.5, 0.0, 0.5) }
    let w = pbpk28_trbdf2_w()
    return (w, w, pbpk28_trbdf2_d())
}

// Predictor pass: step every drug under f_use into ct_pred.
fn md_predict(md: &!MultiDrug28, dt: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let n = (*md).n
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        md_load(md, i)
        md_kernel_loaded(md, i, dt)
        // The predictor's stages are stages of this step too: fold their most
        // negative entry in before sc_w is reused, or md_neg_min_rel misses a
        // negative that only the predictor produced (PR #2695 review).
        if (*md).method != 1 {
            if (*md).sc_w.neg_min_rel < (*md).neg_min_rel[i] { (*md).neg_min_rel[i] = (*md).sc_w.neg_min_rel }
        }
        var o: i32 = 0
        while o < 14 {
            (*md).ct_pred[i * 14 + o] = (*md).sc_s.ct[o]
            o = o + 1
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
}

// Absorption for this step: removes the absorbed mass from each lumen and sets
// the constant gut-tissue input rate (mg/h) per drug.
fn md_absorb(md: &!MultiDrug28, dt: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let n = (*md).n
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        let lum = (*md).lumen[i]
        if lum > 0.0 {
            let absorbed = lum * md_absorbed_fraction((*md).ka[i] * dt)
            (*md).lumen[i] = lum - absorbed
            (*md).gut_rate[i] = absorbed / dt
        } else {
            (*md).gut_rate[i] = 0.0
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
}

// Corrector pass: advances every drug from t_n under f_use and books
// elimination, dose and AUC with the step's own quadrature weights, then
// clears the drug's restart flag.
fn md_advance(md: &!MultiDrug28, dt: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let n = (*md).n
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        md_load(md, i)
        md_kernel_loaded(md, i, dt)
        let (w0, wg, w1) = md_weights(md, i)
        let cl = (*md).sc_p.cl_central
        // Accumulate into locals and check before writing: the state is finite
        // (the kernel checks it), but the cumulative sums can still overflow
        // over many steps (AUC grows without bound in a closed system).
        let e_new = (*md).elim[i] + pbpk28_hepatic_elim_quad_ws(&(*md).sc_s, &(*md).sc_w, cl, &(*md).sc_h, dt, w0, wg, w1)
        let d_new = (*md).dose_in[i] + dt * (*md).sc_i.in_b
        let a_new = (*md).auc_b[i] + pbpk28_hepatic_auc_quad_ws(&(*md).sc_s, &(*md).sc_w, dt, w0, wg, w1)
        let c_new = (*md).clamped[i] + (*md).sc_w.clamped
        if !(is_finite_f64(e_new) && is_finite_f64(d_new) && is_finite_f64(a_new) && is_finite_f64(c_new)) {
            panic("multidrug28: step accounting (elimination, dose, AUC) would overflow")
        }
        (*md).elim[i] = e_new
        (*md).dose_in[i] = d_new
        (*md).auc_b[i] = a_new
        (*md).clamped[i] = c_new
        if (*md).method != 1 {
            if (*md).sc_w.neg_min_rel < (*md).neg_min_rel[i] { (*md).neg_min_rel[i] = (*md).sc_w.neg_min_rel }
        }
        (*md).restart[i] = 0.0
        var o: i32 = 0
        while o < 14 {
            (*md).cv[i * 14 + o] = (*md).sc_s.cv[o]
            (*md).ct[i * 14 + o] = (*md).sc_s.ct[o]
            o = o + 1
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
}

// One coupled step of length dt with md.iters coupling sweeps (see header).
fn md_coupled_step(md: &!MultiDrug28, dt: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    md_absorb(md, dt)
    md_factors_into(md, false, false)
    md_set_f_use(md, false)
    var sweep: i32 = 0
    while sweep < (*md).iters {
        md_predict(md, dt)
        md_factors_into(md, true, true)
        md_set_f_use(md, true)
        sweep = sweep + 1
    }
    md_advance(md, dt)
}

// A step must leave every drug's blood concentration finite. A finite but
// absurd dt still overflows the kernel's coefficients (h·Q/V and friends), and
// Inf/Inf or Inf-Inf then yields NaN: measured 2026-09-26, dt = 1e300 returned
// a NaN body mass with no error, and NaN spreads through the blood row on the
// next mixing step. Checking the 16 blood entries fails that closed instead of
// handing back a number that is not one; the deep state is reached through
// blood, so a NaN anywhere surfaces here within a step or two.
fn md_check_finite_blood(md: &MultiDrug28) with Mut, Panic {
    let n = (*md).n
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        if !is_finite_f64((*md).cv[i * 14]) { panic("multidrug28: step produced a non-finite blood concentration (dt too large?)") }
        i = i + 1
    }
}

// Configuration check made by every md_step, exposed so that a gate can test
// it (a panic cannot be observed by the run-pass harness). Returns 0 when the
// configuration is valid, 1 for an unknown md.method, 2 for md.iters < 0: a
// negative sweep count ran zero sweeps and silently fell back to Lie coupling
// (measured 2026-09-27: iters = -1 gave a victim AUC bit-identical to
// iters = 0; PR #2695 review).
pub fn md_config_error(md: &MultiDrug28) -> i32 {
    if !((*md).method == 0 || (*md).method == 1) { return 1 }
    if (*md).iters < 0 { return 2 }
    return 0
}

// One coupled step from t to the representable time t_next > t. The step is
// integrated over the ACTUAL clock delta h = fl(t_next - t), never over a
// requested dt: transport, absorption, infusion, AUC and elimination all use
// h, and the clock then becomes t_next. So the integrated time and the clock
// advance agree (PR #2695 review: at t = 2^53, fl(t + 3) = t + 4, and a step
// integrated over 3 h while the clock moved 4 h, so an infusion delivered 3 mg
// for 4 h of clock). The subtraction is exact whenever t >= t_next - t
// (Sterbenz), which covers every step after the first on any grid; otherwise
// it carries one rounding, <= ulp(h)/2. The clock update is checked before
// anything is mutated: t_next must be finite and ahead of t, so h > 0.
fn md_step_to(md: &!MultiDrug28, t_next: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let t = (*md).t
    if !(is_finite_f64(t_next) && t_next > t) { panic("multidrug28: md_step: t + dt is not finite or does not advance t") }
    let h = t_next - t
    let cfg = md_config_error(md)
    if cfg == 1 { panic("multidrug28: md.method must be md_method_trbdf2() or md_method_cn_legacy()") }
    if cfg == 2 { panic("multidrug28: md.iters must be >= 0 (0 Lie, 1 predictor-corrector, >1 iterated)") }
    md_coupled_step(md, h)
    md_check_finite_blood(md)
    (*md).t = t_next
    (*md).stepped = 1.0
}

// Advances the clock to fl(t + dt) and integrates the step over the actual
// clock delta h = fl(t + dt) - t (md_step_to), which differs from dt by the
// rounding of the clock addition: |h - dt| <= ulp(t + dt)/2. At ordinary
// clocks that is a relative 1.1e-16 of dt, or nothing; at t = 2^53 with
// dt = 3 it is h = 4. t + dt can overflow to +Inf (two steps of 1e308), and
// at a large t a small dt is absorbed by round-off (t + dt == t, h = 0),
// which would leave md_run_to looping forever: both panic before anything is
// mutated.
pub fn md_step(md: &!MultiDrug28, dt: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    if !(is_finite_f64(dt) && dt > 0.0) { panic("multidrug28: md_step needs a finite dt > 0") }
    md_step_to(md, (*md).t + dt)
}

// Advances to exactly t_end with steps of dt. A full step is taken only while
// its endpoint on the actual clock does not pass the target, fl(t + dt) <=
// t_end, compared exactly. Then whatever is left, rem = t_end - t, is
// integrated as one more step whenever it is positive. No tolerance is
// involved: because no full step passes t_end, rem >= 0, and a positive rem
// between two representable times is at least one ulp of t, so the step
// always advances the clock. Every hour of clock is therefore integrated, and
// an infusion delivers exactly (to the rounding of each step) its rate times
// the clock advance. The cost is that clock drift from accumulating t + dt
// can leave a remainder of a few ulps, which is integrated as a tiny step
// (e.g. ten steps of 0.1 from 0 end at 0.9999999999999999, and the 1.1e-16 h
// left is stepped). That is harmless, and it is the price of never discarding
// time. Earlier versions discarded remainders they judged to be round-off,
// and every such rule dropped real time somewhere: a 1e-9·dt snap lost a
// 5e-10 h remainder, a count fixed from span/dt overshot at t0 = 2^53, and a
// drift allowance skipped 2 h of a 6 h target at t0 = 2^53 with dt = 4
// (4 mg infused for 6 h of a 1 mg/h infusion; PR #2695 review).
// Consequences for grid targets: (0.6, 0.02) is 30 steps, 29 of dt and a
// last remainder 0.6 - t, because thirty accumulated steps of 0.02 put the
// clock at 0.6000000000000002, past 0.6. (0.61, 0.02) is 30 steps plus a
// 0.01 remainder, and (1.0000000005, 1.0) is a 1.0 step plus a 5e-10 step.
// A dt far larger than the span takes one step of the whole span.
// Every step, full or remainder, integrates the actual clock delta, not the
// requested dt (md_step_to): a full step integrates h = fl(t + dt) - t, with
// |h - dt| <= ulp(t + dt)/2, and the remainder step goes to t_end exactly and
// integrates h = fl(t_end - t), exact when t >= t_end/2 and otherwise within
// ulp(h)/2 of the true delta. At t = 2^53, run_to(t + 4, dt 3) is one step
// that the clock rounds to 4 h, and it integrates 4 h. At ordinary clocks h
// equals dt or differs from it in the last bit.
// A non-finite t_end (NaN, +-Inf) panics, as does a non-finite or
// non-positive dt. A finite target not strictly ahead of t is a no-op, so
// the clock never moves backwards. The run ends with t == t_end exactly.
// Spacing of the doubles in the binade of y >= 0 (finite): ulp(y) = 2^e·2^-52
// for 2^e <= y < 2^(e+1) normal, and 2^-1074 below the normal range. The
// power of two is found by halving or doubling from 1, which is exact.
fn md_ulp(y: f64) -> f64 with Mut {
    if y < 2.2250738585072014e-308 { return 4.9406564584124654e-324 }
    var p = 1.0
    if y >= 1.0 {
        while p * 2.0 <= y { p = p * 2.0 }
    } else {
        while p > y { p = p * 0.5 }
    }
    return p * 2.220446049250313e-16
}

// Argument check of md_run_to, exposed so that a gate can test it (a panic
// cannot be observed by the run-pass harness): 0 valid, 1 dt not a finite
// positive number, 2 t_end not finite, 3 dt below the clock's resolution
// somewhere on the way to a target ahead of t, 4 the current clock not
// finite. md_run_to refuses on any nonzero code before any step, so nothing
// is mutated. It deliberately does
// not substitute a coarser step: that would change the integrator's
// resolution without saying so.
// Code 3 must hold for the whole run, not only at the starting clock (PR
// #2695 review): from t = 2^53 - 1 toward 2^53 + 2 with dt = 1, the first
// step is fine (ulp 1) and lands on 2^53, where fl(2^53 + 1) = 2^53 (ulp 2,
// ties to even), so the next md_step panicked after the first had already
// mutated the state. The check is therefore made where resolution is
// coarsest. Every clock value x at which a full step can be taken lies in
// [t, t_end]: steps only move forward, the loop steps only while
// fl(x + dt) <= t_end, and a step that does not advance leaves x <= t_end.
// So |x| <= Y = max(|t|, |t_end|), and since the spacing of doubles is
// non-decreasing in |x|, the gap from x to its upper neighbour is at most
// ulp(Y) (for x < 0 it can only be smaller). If dt > ulp(Y)/2, then x + dt
// lies strictly beyond the midpoint between x and that neighbour, so
// fl(x + dt) is at least the neighbour and exceeds x: every full step
// advances the clock. The strict inequality is needed: at dt = ulp/2 exactly
// the tie goes to the even neighbour, which is x itself half of the time, so
// testing fl(x + dt) > x at one point would pass or fail by parity. The
// remainder step then goes to t_end itself (md_step_to), which is ahead of
// the clock, so it lands on t_end exactly and integrates h > 0.
// Code 4: the current clock is not finite (PR #2695 review). md.t is a public
// field; with t = NaN every comparison is false, so md_run_to returned
// without stepping and reported nothing, and t = -Inf reached md_ulp(+Inf),
// whose doubling loop never ends.
pub fn md_run_to_error(md: &MultiDrug28, t_end: f64, dt: f64) -> i32 with Mut {
    if !(is_finite_f64(dt) && dt > 0.0) { return 1 }
    if !(is_finite_f64(t_end)) { return 2 }
    let t = (*md).t
    if !(is_finite_f64(t)) { return 4 }
    if t_end > t {
        let at = if t < 0.0 { 0.0 - t } else { t }
        let ae = if t_end < 0.0 { 0.0 - t_end } else { t_end }
        let y = if at > ae { at } else { ae }
        if !(dt > 0.5 * md_ulp(y)) { return 3 }
    }
    return 0
}

pub fn md_run_to(md: &!MultiDrug28, t_end: f64, dt: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let e = md_run_to_error(md, t_end, dt)
    if e == 1 { panic("multidrug28: md_run_to needs a finite dt > 0") }
    if e == 2 { panic("multidrug28: md_run_to needs a finite t_end") }
    if e == 3 { panic("multidrug28: md_run_to: dt below clock resolution between t and t_end (dt <= ulp/2); refusing rather than stepping coarser") }
    if e == 4 { panic("multidrug28: md_run_to: the current clock md.t is not finite") }
    if !(t_end > (*md).t) { return }
    while (*md).t + dt <= t_end {
        md_step(md, dt)
    }
    if t_end > (*md).t {
        md_step_to(md, t_end)
    }
}

// Mass currently in the body (all organs, both layers) for drug i.
// An unregistered slot below capacity would reconstruct a zero state and
// report a plausible 0.0, so the index is validated like the setters'.
pub fn md_body_mass(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    return pbpk28_total_mass(md_state_of(md, i), md_params_of(md, i))
}

// |body + lumen + lost + eliminated - administered| / administered for drug i.
pub fn md_mass_residual(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    let d = (*md).dose_in[i]
    if d <= 0.0 { return 0.0 }
    let m = md_body_mass(md, i) + (*md).lumen[i] + (*md).lost[i] + (*md).elim[i]
    let r = (m - d) / d
    return if r < 0.0 { 0.0 - r } else { r }
}

// Mass (mg) the negativity clamp has added to drug i so far (legacy CN path;
// always 0 on the default TR-BDF2 path, which has no clamp). Mass balance and
// the discrete AUC identity are exact only while this is zero.
pub fn md_clamped(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> f64 with Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    return (*md).clamped[i]
}

// Most negative entry of any stage or endpoint of drug i so far, relative to
// its step's scale (default path; 0 when none was negative), counting the
// predictor passes of every coupling sweep as well as the corrector. The kernel
// panics below -tol, so a finished run has this >= -tol of every step.
pub fn md_neg_min_rel(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32) -> f64 with Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    return (*md).neg_min_rel[i]
}

// Current competitive factor seen by victim i at (site, enz).
// All three codes are validated: site 2 would otherwise alias the next victim's
// factor, and an unregistered victim would return an initialised scratch value.
pub fn md_factor_now(md: &MultiDrug28, i: i32, site: i32, enz: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    md_check_drug(md, i)
    md_check_site(site)
    md_check_enz(enz)
    return 1.0 / (1.0 + md_site_load(md, false, i, site, enz))
}
